sequenceDiagram
  actor Player
  participant Engine as BYOND callback
  participant Atom as atom.Click
  participant Mob as mob.ClickOn
  participant Target as target subtype
  participant Item as held item subtype
  Player->>Engine: click atom / browser link
  alt Atom click
    Engine->>Atom: Click(location, control, params)
    Atom->>Mob: usr.ClickOn(src, params)
    Mob->>Mob: target + click clock + modifiers
    alt Modifier shortcut
      Mob->>Target: modifier-specific dispatch
    else Ordinary action
      Mob->>Mob: special equipment, incapacitation, movement gates
      alt Held item + suitable range
        Mob->>Target: attackby(item, actor)
        Mob->>Item: afterattack(target, actor, adjacency, params)
      else Empty hand / ranged action
        Mob->>Target: UnarmedAttack or RangedAttack routing
      end
    end
  else Browser href
    Engine->>Engine: client.Topic validates usr matches mob
    Engine->>Target: parent/native href target dispatch
  end
  Note over Mob,Item: Overrides, queued spawn callbacks and early returns change concrete paths. See exact source, not this abstraction, for authorization order.
